WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.130
- We always like to finish
up with something cool

00:00:02.130 --> 00:00:04.429
trending on social media,
this is what I'm liking.

00:00:04.429 --> 00:00:07.470
(rock music)

00:00:07.470 --> 00:00:09.960
A Chicago woman is using
her love of crocheting

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:11.370
and her passion for her community

00:00:11.370 --> 00:00:12.840
to make a real statement.

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:14.820
She launched her own
handmade clothing brand

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:16.350
called T'KOR Couture,

00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:17.910
and she calls it the intersection

00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:19.890
of fashion and the Civil Rights movement.

00:00:19.890 --> 00:00:22.800
We have her on the line watching
on NBC Chicago right now.

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:24.381
What's up, Dinah?

00:00:24.381 --> 00:00:25.710
(audience cheering)

00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:26.543
- Hi Kelly.

00:00:26.543 --> 00:00:28.350
I'm so excited to be here.

00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:29.790
- Oh my God, I'm so excited as well.

00:00:29.790 --> 00:00:31.890
You're getting real
traction on social media.

00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:33.660
So what inspired your line?

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:37.830
- So I taught myself to crochet
when I was 12 years old.

00:00:37.830 --> 00:00:40.950
Just started off with
a basic hat, scarves.

00:00:40.950 --> 00:00:42.480
And a few years passed,

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:45.390
and I really wanted to
stretch my crochet abilities,

00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:48.930
and so, I happened to stumble
onto this Facebook page

00:00:48.930 --> 00:00:51.750
that was just full of other Black woman

00:00:51.750 --> 00:00:53.700
crocheting real clothing.

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:56.130
And so, it just really opened up my mind

00:00:56.130 --> 00:00:57.291
to the possibilities.

00:00:57.291 --> 00:00:59.730
And so, this was really reinforced

00:00:59.730 --> 00:01:02.160
when I went to the University of Chicago.

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:04.500
I decided to major in sociology,

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:08.040
and I just learned so
much about my heritage

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:10.110
and how it related to fashion.

00:01:10.110 --> 00:01:12.630
Like how the Black
Panther Party used dress

00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:17.430
as a tool to push its political agenda.

00:01:17.430 --> 00:01:18.263
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:18.263 --> 00:01:21.840
- And so, I really just feel
very much inspired by that

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:25.200
and want to use that in my own crocheting

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:28.980
as I continue to uplift the
stories from communities

00:01:28.980 --> 00:01:31.080
that often go unheard.

00:01:31.080 --> 00:01:32.280
- Man, it's so cool.

00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:34.170
I just, I don't believe in art

00:01:34.170 --> 00:01:37.140
unless it has messaging behind
it, whatever the message is.

00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:40.830
And I think it's so cool
how your line works.

00:01:40.830 --> 00:01:42.630
It's just, it's an
incredibly inspiring thing.

00:01:42.630 --> 00:01:44.970
So talk us through some of your work.

00:01:44.970 --> 00:01:47.220
- Yeah, so one of the projects

00:01:47.220 --> 00:01:49.567
that I'm really proud of
was inspired by the book

00:01:49.567 --> 00:01:52.440
"The Colored Girls" by Ntozake Shange.

00:01:52.440 --> 00:01:54.780
And this is basically a story

00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:57.210
about a lot of different woman of color

00:01:57.210 --> 00:02:00.660
each representing a color,
red, blue, green, et cetera.

00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:02.460
And so I took these characters

00:02:02.460 --> 00:02:05.340
and their stories and made
an outfit for each of them.

00:02:05.340 --> 00:02:08.700
I also love my fluffy bucket hats.

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:11.160
I made these just because I was tired

00:02:11.160 --> 00:02:14.220
of having hats that didn't
necessarily fit my head.

00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:18.000
And so, I love to wear protective
styles and my big afro,

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:22.770
and I just wanted a hat that
was as versatile as my hair.

00:02:22.770 --> 00:02:23.967
- Yeah.

00:02:23.967 --> 00:02:28.380
- And finally one of the
people that truly inspire me

00:02:28.380 --> 00:02:31.290
is artist Jean-Michel Basquiat.

00:02:31.290 --> 00:02:35.070
He is known for his crown symbol,

00:02:35.070 --> 00:02:37.830
which he placed on Black icons

00:02:37.830 --> 00:02:42.069
to redefine the notion of race and power.

00:02:42.069 --> 00:02:45.720
And so, I use the crown
motif in my own work

00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:48.870
in an effort to continue
to uplift the stories

00:02:48.870 --> 00:02:50.790
coming from communities of color.

00:02:50.790 --> 00:02:53.823
- You are incredibly cool, ma'am.

00:02:54.660 --> 00:02:55.890
Oh my gosh.

00:02:55.890 --> 00:02:58.770
Like that whole ass look too is so rad.

00:02:58.770 --> 00:03:00.810
I thank you so much, Dinah.

00:03:00.810 --> 00:03:02.850
You're incredibly gifted.

00:03:02.850 --> 00:03:04.200
Keep inspiring us.

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:06.240
I'm liking your posts
right now, all right.

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:07.440
- [Dinah] Thank you.

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:08.370
- And that's not all, ma'am.

00:03:08.370 --> 00:03:09.900
Our season long partner Pilot Pen

00:03:09.900 --> 00:03:11.760
makers of FriXion, the go-to erasable pen

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:12.810
of "The Kelly Clarkson Show"

00:03:12.810 --> 00:03:15.930
want to celebrate those creating
fearlessly just like you.

00:03:15.930 --> 00:03:17.430
So, they're gonna give you $1,000.

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:18.338
How's that sound?

00:03:18.338 --> 00:03:21.019
(audience cheering)

00:03:21.019 --> 00:03:23.245
- Thank you.

00:03:23.245 --> 00:03:24.078
I appreciate that.

00:03:24.078 --> 00:03:24.911
- Oh my gosh.

00:03:24.911 --> 00:03:25.830
You're so cool, Dinah.

00:03:25.830 --> 00:03:27.840
I can't wait to see what you do next.

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:28.673
Incredible.

00:03:28.673 --> 00:03:29.596
Thank you so much.

00:03:29.596 --> 00:03:31.001
And thank you to all our guests this hour,

00:03:31.001 --> 00:03:35.760
Shania Twain, Kylen, Anali,
Niteri, Alana, and Chris Powell.

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:36.641
Y'all have a great day.

00:03:36.641 --> 00:03:38.613
And if it's not, try and change it.

